# CLI Development Guidelines

## Commander.js Usage

- **Command Structure**: Use Commander.js for CLI command definitions in [src/bin/muti-ports.ts](mdc:src/bin/muti-ports.ts)
- **Option Parsing**: Always validate required options and provide helpful error messages
- **Help Text**: Provide clear, concise help text for each command
- **Exit Codes**: Use appropriate exit codes (0 for success, 1 for errors)

## User Experience

- **Interactive Prompts**: Use Inquirer.js for complex user input when needed
- **Color Output**: Use Chalk for colored output to improve readability
- **Progress Indicators**: Show progress for long-running operations
- **Error Messages**: Provide actionable error messages with suggestions

## Command Organization

- **Grouping**: Group related commands logically
- **Aliases**: Provide short aliases for common commands
- **Defaults**: Set sensible defaults for optional parameters
- **Validation**: Validate input parameters before processing

## Internationalization

- **User Messages**: All user-facing text should use the i18n system from [src/i18n/index.ts](mdc:src/i18n/index.ts)
- **Language Detection**: Respect user's language preference
- **Fallbacks**: Provide English fallbacks for missing translations
- **Consistency**: Use consistent terminology across all languages

## Testing CLI Commands

- **Mock Input**: Test commands with various input combinations
- **Error Cases**: Test error handling and edge cases
- **Integration**: Test command interactions and data flow
